From 751abfe40949c48a012f65dc98b30d96f46b8049 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pi OAuth Compatibility Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 20:09:25 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ai): update Claude Code protocol to 2.1.280

Anthropic now rejects Opus 5.5 requests that advertise Claude Code
2.1.258 with claude_code_version_too_old. Advertise 2.1.280, which
keeps the same billing salt and request shape.

The 2.1.280 cch billing checksum moved out of the JavaScript bundle:
the billing header is built with a literal cch=00000 placeholder and
the real value is injected by native runtime code, so the previous
seeded XXH64 body patch no longer reproduces it. Live verification
against api.anthropic.com (2026-09-23) shows the API accepts the
well-formed zero value, so the billing header now emits cch=00000
directly and the serialized request body is forwarded unchanged.
